# Gray-flow: re-check the verdict URL on returning launches

Once an install has been routed into the gray (web) part, the app must NOT
blindly reopen the previously saved URL forever. On every subsequent launch
(AppMode.online / LaunchMode.web) the app must:

1. Query the config endpoint again (same attribution POST body).
2. If the backend returns a fresh `ok: true` + `url`, open THAT url in the
   WebView — even if it differs from the previously cached one (the offer /
   landing URL can rotate on the backend side).
3. Persist the new url + expiry, replacing the old cached value.
4. Only fall back to the cached url when the request fails or there is no
   network (an expired cached url is still better than a blank screen).

Push URLs keep priority: a one-shot push URL (cold-start tap) is consumed and
opened first, before the normal config re-check.

Rationale: the partner landing URL changes over time. A returning user must
always land on the current URL, not a stale one captured at first launch.

Implementation note: keep the re-check cheap (short attribution wait on
returning launches) so total load time stays under the 10s budget.
